# L3: BOTH BARS, audits off (c2-packed-tp4-lanes-time-gate). The gate's lanes-timing plan, four arms, one boot each: one fast user
# (user 0, marked with vllm_xargs qwen_lane=fast) beside 3 standard users at 4,096 tokens, beside 2, beside 1, and beside 3 at 32,768;
# real text to its natural end (tau on real coding text is what the bars hang on, so no stream is forced past its EOS). The ratio is swept
# on every boot by QWEN_FAST_LANE_SCHEDULE (k = 0, 0.5, 1, 1.5, 2 for 25 frames each with every lane live, then the controller), so a
# boot gives the fast and standard rates at five fixed ratios and under the controller.
# Product, per arm and stretch (lanes_report): the fast user's and every standard user's steady rate over the frame (tokens over the
# summed cycle of EVERY round in the stretch, the other lane's included), P, F, the switch cost sigma, tau per lane, and the design's frame
# arithmetic beside them; then per standard-user count the best stretch and MET / MISSED against 150 / 75. A missed bar is a result, not a
# failure: the plan is PASS when every arm was healthy and read, NOT_EXERCISED where a stretch had too few rounds. The client's own chunk
# timeline gives the same rates over the window in which every stream was live (a check that shares none of the log parsing).
# SOFT: a failing arm is data; the window goes on.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card lanes window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it
# over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/lanes and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig,
# a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image L0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# C2_GATE_JIT=record as in L1.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; per arm an engine build 3-8 min plus 3-10 min of streams (up to 4,096 tokens per user at 75-170
# tok/s, four serial prefills first: 30 s at 4,096, 2 min at 32,768): 30-70 min for four arms. Step limit 380 min; worst case 248 min.
# Read: the "lanes ratio=... n=..." rows and the "TARGET n=..." rows; tau (real coding text) beside the fixture's 12.1: the minimum tau
# for both bars at the levers in the branch is the table in docs/tp4-lanes-window.md.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-lanes-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate
C2_GATE_PLAN=lanes-timing
C2_GATE_JIT=record
